  free: {
    balloondog:["Metal Balloon Dog · Multi-angle Sheet","An original sheet with front, side, 3/4, top, back and detail views. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Chrome is 'a picture of its surroundings'. Block in the dark reflected bands before the highlights.","The highlights break at each balloon joint. Think of the body as several spheres.","Add the blue reflected light on the floor and the metal feel really comes alive."]],
    tiger:["Tiger · Analysis Board","An original board with observation references, form details (eyes, nose, paws enlarged), a 3-step sketch method, texture and color, and usage tips. No watermark.",["Block in the body first as one big forward-leaning mass, then divide the shoulder and front paws.","Stripes should curve with the round surface of the body to feel three-dimensional.","Keep the white fur (above the eyes, cheeks, chest) between the orange fur to sharpen the face."]],
    deer:["Red Deer · 7 Individual Cuts + Analysis Board","Originals of 7 cuts (roaring hero, front, 3/4, side, back, top, fur detail) and the analysis board. All files have no watermark.",["Draw antlers from large branches to small ones, breaking them up like a single tree.","Don't draw the mane hair by hair. Split it into dark and light masses first.","Compare antler span and body length with the top view to get front proportions right."]],
    rooster:["Rooster · 8 Individual Cuts + Analysis Board","Originals of 8 cuts (dynamic side, front, 3/4, top, back, face close-up, feather texture, walking) and the analysis board. No watermark.",["Don't draw tail feathers one by one. Block large curved masses first, then separate the overlaps.","Compare body and tail length in the top view to get the side-profile proportions.","Keep the color contrast of the red comb and the deep teal tail to make the picture pop."]],
    pig:["Pig · Analysis Board","An original board with observation references, form details (close-ups), a 3-step sketch method, texture and color, and usage tips. No watermark.",["Block in the outer mass first, divide ears, snout and legs, then build the shading.","The snout is two nostrils and a moist highlight; the feet are split hooves.","Add a very faint bounce light from the floor under the belly so the mass doesn't float."]],
    grinder:["Grinder · Multi-angle Sheet","An original sheet with the grinder from front, side, top and detail views. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Divide it into three masses first: handle, body and round blade cover.","Separate the gloss of the metal blade and plastic body with value contrast.","The round blade turns into an ellipse depending on the view, so check the tilt of the ellipse first."]],
    cherrykettle:["Cherry × Kettle · Multi-angle Sheet","An original combo-subject sheet with a shiny kettle and a cherry. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Block in the surroundings reflected on the kettle as large masses and save the highlights for last.","The red of the cherry against the gray of the metal is the point. Show the size difference with the cherry stem's shadow.","Don't overdo droplets: just 2–3, drawn as a bright dot with a dark edge."]],
    faucet:["Faucet × Red Marble · Multi-angle Sheet","An original sheet with a shiny chrome faucet and a red marble from several angles. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Chrome is 'a picture of its surroundings'. Block in the dark reflected bands before the bright faces.","The red marble gets its transparent depth from one highlight and the reflected light on the floor.","The handle direction changes with each angle, so line up the center axis of the cylinder first."]],
    glasscherry:["Glass Cherry · Multi-angle Sheet","An original sheet with a glass-like transparent cherry from several angles. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Transparent objects show what is behind them. Be sure to include the bright caustic inside the floor shadow.","Draw surface droplets simply as a bright dot plus a dark edge.","The stem is a thin curved cylinder. Add life with the brown shift at its tip."]],
    ram:["Mountain Goat · Multi-angle Sheet","An original sheet with the mountain goat, curled horns and thick fur, from several angles. A high-resolution file with no watermark.",["Set the spiral direction of the horn first, then repeat the ridge wrinkles along the curve.","Don't draw fur hair by hair: go masses → flow direction → clean-up of the ends.","The legs are thin compared with the body. Finish them firmly with the split hooves."]]
  }
